IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc8-part8-assaults`

-- ccc8-tests-part8-assaults.l4 -- tests for ccc8-part8-assaults.l4 (sections 264 to 269.1). Expected values are written by hand from the text.
-- The stand-in below is NOT the penalty of section 787(1) (outside this part): it states nothing, so only the limb of this part is tested.
`s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 264 -- criminal harassment`

-- (2) "The conduct ... consists of doing any of the following ...: (a) repeatedly following ...; (a.1) monitoring ...; (b) repeatedly communicating ...; (c) besetting or watching the dwelling-house ...; or (d) engaging in threatening conduct"
--                                                                                       (a)   (a.1) (b)   (c)   (d)
#ASSERT `s 264(2) the conduct is the prohibited conduct mentioned in subsection (1)` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264(2) the conduct is the prohibited conduct mentioned in subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264(2) the conduct is the prohibited conduct mentioned in subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264(2) the conduct is the prohibited conduct mentioned in subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264(2) the conduct is the prohibited conduct mentioned in subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264(2) the conduct is the prohibited conduct mentioned in subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6) "a person's safety includes their psychological safety"
#ASSERT `s 264(6) a person's safety includes their psychological safety` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264(6) a person's safety includes their psychological safety` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) "Everyone commits an offence who, with intent to harass another person or knowing that, or being reckless as to whether, they would be harassing another person, engages without lawful authority in conduct referred to in subsection (2) if, in all the circumstances, the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause that other person to believe that the other person's safety ... is threatened"
--                                                          intent knows reckless conduct       no authority expectation
#ASSERT `s 264(1) the person commits the offence of criminal harassment` TRUE  FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE)  TRUE TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264(1) the person commits the offence of criminal harassment` FALSE TRUE  FALSE (JUST TRUE)  TRUE TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264(1) the person commits the offence of criminal harassment` FALSE FALSE TRUE  (JUST TRUE)  TRUE TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264(1) the person commits the offence of criminal harassment` TRUE  FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE)  TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 264(1) the person commits the offence of criminal harassment` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE)  TRUE TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 264(1) the person commits the offence of criminal harassment` TRUE  FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE)  FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 264(1) the person commits the offence of criminal harassment` TRUE  FALSE FALSE NOTHING      TRUE TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 264(1) the person commits the offence of criminal harassment` TRUE  FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) "guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... not more than 10 years; or (b) summary conviction"
#ASSERT `s 264(3) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 264(3) the punishment` `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
-- (4) "Where a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court ... shall consider as an aggravating factor that, at the time the offence was committed, the person contravened (a) ... an order made under section 161 or a recognizance ...; or (b) ... any other order or recognizance, or of an undertaking"
#ASSERT `s 264(4) the court shall consider the contravention as an aggravating factor` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264(4) the court shall consider the contravention as an aggravating factor` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264(4) the court shall consider the contravention as an aggravating factor` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 264(4) the court shall consider the contravention as an aggravating factor` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 264(4) the duty of the court to consider the contravention` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 264(4) consider the contravention as an aggravating factor` AT 1
-- (5) "Where the court is satisfied of the existence of an aggravating factor referred to in subsection (4), but decides not to give effect to it for sentencing purposes, the court shall give reasons for its decision"
#ASSERT `s 264(5) the court shall give reasons for its decision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264(5) the court shall give reasons for its decision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 264(5) the court shall give reasons for its decision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 264(5) the duty of the court to give reasons` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 264(5) give reasons for deciding not to give effect to the aggravating factor` AT 1

§ `Section 264.1 -- uttering threats`

-- (1) "Everyone commits an offence who, in any manner, knowingly utters, conveys or causes any person to receive a threat (a) to cause death or bodily harm to any person; (b) to burn, destroy or damage real or personal property; or (c) to kill, poison or injure an animal or bird that is the property of any person"
#ASSERT `s 264.1(1) the person commits the offence of uttering threats` `s 264.1(1)(a) a threat to cause death or bodily harm to any person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264.1(1) the person commits the offence of uttering threats` `s 264.1(1)(b) a threat to burn, destroy or damage real or personal property` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264.1(1) the person commits the offence of uttering threats` `s 264.1(1)(c) a threat to kill, poison or injure an animal or bird that is the property of any person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 264.1(1) the person commits the offence of uttering threats` `s 264.1(1)(a) a threat to cause death or bodily harm to any person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 264.1 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
-- (2) for a threat under (1)(a): indictable, not exceeding five years; (3) for a threat under (1)(b) or (c): indictable, not exceeding two years
#ASSERT `s 264.1 the punishment` `s 264.1(1)(a) a threat to cause death or bodily harm to any person` `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
#ASSERT `s 264.1 the punishment` `s 264.1(1)(b) a threat to burn, destroy or damage real or personal property` `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
#ASSERT `s 264.1 the punishment` `s 264.1(1)(c) a threat to kill, poison or injure an animal or bird that is the property of any person` `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`

§ `Section 265 -- assault`

-- (3) "no consent is obtained where the complainant submits or does not resist by reason of (a) the application of force ...; (b) threats or fear of the application of force ...; (c) fraud; or (d) the exercise of authority"
#ASSERT `s 265(3) no consent is obtained` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 265(3) no consent is obtained` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 265(3) no consent is obtained` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 265(3) no consent is obtained` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 265(3) no consent is obtained` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) "A person commits an assault when (a) without the consent of another person, he applies force intentionally to that other person, directly or indirectly; (b) he attempts or threatens, by an act or a gesture, to apply force to another person, if he has, or causes that other person to believe on reasonable grounds that he has, present ability to effect his purpose; or (c) while openly wearing or carrying a weapon or an imitation thereof, he accosts or impedes another person or begs"
--                                          (a) force consents (3)           (b) attempts ability causesBelief (c) weapon accosts
#ASSERT `s 265(1) the person commits an assault` TRUE FALSE NOTHING      FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 265(1) the person commits an assault` TRUE TRUE  (JUST TRUE)  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 265(1) the person commits an assault` TRUE TRUE  NOTHING      FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 265(1) the person commits an assault` FALSE FALSE NOTHING     FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 265(1) the person commits an assault` FALSE FALSE NOTHING     TRUE  TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 265(1) the person commits an assault` FALSE FALSE NOTHING     TRUE  FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 265(1) the person commits an assault` FALSE FALSE NOTHING     TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 265(1) the person commits an assault` FALSE FALSE NOTHING     FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 265(1) the person commits an assault` FALSE FALSE NOTHING     FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 265(1) the person commits an assault` FALSE FALSE NOTHING     FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) "This section applies to all forms of assault, including sexual assault ..."
#ASSERT `s 265(2) section 265 applies to the form of assault` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 265(2) section 265 applies to the form of assault` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) "Where an accused alleges that he believed that the complainant consented ..., a judge, if satisfied that there is sufficient evidence and that, if believed by the jury, the evidence would constitute a defence, shall instruct the jury ..."
#ASSERT `s 265(4) the judge shall instruct the jury to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for the belief` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 265(4) the judge shall instruct the jury to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for the belief` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 265(4) the judge shall instruct the jury to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for the belief` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 265(4) the judge shall instruct the jury to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for the belief` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 265(4) the duty of the judge to instruct the jury` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a judge` DOES `s 265(4) instruct the jury to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for the belief` AT 1

§ `Sections 266 to 269`

-- 266 "Every one who commits an assault is guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... not exceeding five years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction"
#ASSERT `s 266 the person commits the offence of assault` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 266 the person commits the offence of assault` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 266 the person commits the offence of assault` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 266 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 266 the punishment` `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
-- 267 "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence ... not more than 10 years or ... summary conviction who, in committing an assault, (a) carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon or an imitation thereof, (b) causes bodily harm to the complainant, or (c) chokes, suffocates or strangles the complainant"
--                                                                                           assault      weapon       imitation bodily harm   chokes
#ASSERT `s 267 the person commits the offence of assault with a weapon or causing bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING      FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267 the person commits the offence of assault with a weapon or causing bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING     TRUE  NOTHING      FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267 the person commits the offence of assault with a weapon or causing bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING     FALSE (JUST TRUE)  FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267 the person commits the offence of assault with a weapon or causing bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING     FALSE NOTHING      TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267 the person commits the offence of assault with a weapon or causing bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING     FALSE NOTHING      FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 267 the person commits the offence of assault with a weapon or causing bodily harm` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING     FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 267 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 267 the punishment` `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
-- 268(3) "'wounds' or 'maims' includes to excise, infibulate or mutilate ..., except where (a) a surgical procedure is performed, by a person duly qualified by provincial law to practise medicine, for the benefit of the physical health ... ; or (b) the person is at least eighteen years of age and there is no resulting bodily harm"
--                                                                                    excision surgical 18+   no harm
#ASSERT `s 268(3) "wounds" or "maims" includes the excision, infibulation or mutilation` TRUE  FALSE    FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 268(3) "wounds" or "maims" includes the excision, infibulation or mutilation` TRUE  TRUE     FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 268(3) "wounds" or "maims" includes the excision, infibulation or mutilation` TRUE  FALSE    TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 268(3) "wounds" or "maims" includes the excision, infibulation or mutilation` TRUE  FALSE    TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 268(3) "wounds" or "maims" includes the excision, infibulation or mutilation` TRUE  FALSE    FALSE TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 268(3) "wounds" or "maims" includes the excision, infibulation or mutilation` FALSE FALSE    FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 268(1) "Every one commits an aggravated assault who wounds, maims, disfigures or endangers the life of the complainant"
#ASSERT `s 268(1) the person commits an aggravated assault` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 268(1) the person commits an aggravated assault` NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 268(1) the person commits an aggravated assault` NOTHING FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 268(1) the person commits an aggravated assault` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 268(1) the person commits an aggravated assault` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 268(2) "guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years"
#ASSERT `s 268(2) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `s 268(2) the punishment` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 14, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
-- 268(4) "no consent to the excision, infibulation or mutilation ... is valid, except in the cases described in paragraphs (3)(a) and (b)"
#ASSERT `s 268(4) the consent is valid` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 268(4) the consent is valid` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 268(4) the consent is valid` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 268.1(2) "sterilization procedure means the severing, clipping, tying or cauterizing, in whole or in part, of the Fallopian tubes, ovaries or uterus of a person or any other procedure ... that results in the permanent prevention of reproduction"; (1) "a sterilization procedure is an act that wounds or maims a person for the purposes of subsection 268(1)"
#ASSERT `s 268.1(2) sterilization procedure` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 268.1(2) sterilization procedure` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 268.1(2) sterilization procedure` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 268.1(1) the act wounds or maims a person for the purposes of subsection 268(1)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 268.1(1) the act wounds or maims a person for the purposes of subsection 268(1)` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 268.1(1) the act wounds or maims a person for the purposes of subsection 268(1)` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 269 "Every one who unlawfully causes bodily harm to any person is guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... ten years; or (b) summary conviction"
#ASSERT `s 269 the person commits the offence of unlawfully causing bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 269 the person commits the offence of unlawfully causing bodily harm` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 269 the person commits the offence of unlawfully causing bodily harm` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 269 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 269 the punishment` `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 266 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`

§ `Sections 269.01 and 269.1`

-- 269.01(2) "public transit employee means an individual who works for, or is contracted to work for, an organization that provides passenger transportation services to the public"; "vehicle includes a bus, paratransit vehicle, licensed taxi cab, train, subway, tram and ferry"
#ASSERT `s 269.01(2) public transit employee` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 269.01(2) public transit employee` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 269.01(2) vehicle` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 269.01(2) vehicle` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 269.01(1) "When a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in paragraph 264.1(1)(a) or any of sections 266 to 269, it shall consider as an aggravating circumstance the fact that the victim of the offence was, at the time of the commission of the offence, a public transit employee engaged in the performance of his or her duty"
#ASSERT `s 269.01(1) the court shall consider the fact as an aggravating circumstance` (`Provision of the Code` OF 266, "") (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 269.01(1) the court shall consider the fact as an aggravating circumstance` (`Provision of the Code` OF 267, "") (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 269.01(1) the court shall consider the fact as an aggravating circumstance` (`Provision of the Code` OF 268, "(1)") (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 269.01(1) the court shall consider the fact as an aggravating circumstance` (`Provision of the Code` OF 269, "") (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 269.01(1) the court shall consider the fact as an aggravating circumstance` (`Provision of the Code` OF 264.1, "(1)(a)") (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 269.01(1) the court shall consider the fact as an aggravating circumstance` (`Provision of the Code` OF 264.1, "(1)(b)") (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 269.01(1) the court shall consider the fact as an aggravating circumstance` (`Provision of the Code` OF 265, "") (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 269.01(1) the court shall consider the fact as an aggravating circumstance` (`Provision of the Code` OF 270, "") (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 269.01(1) the court shall consider the fact as an aggravating circumstance` (`Provision of the Code` OF 266, "") (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 269.01(1) the court shall consider the fact as an aggravating circumstance` (`Provision of the Code` OF 266, "") (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 269.01(1) the duty of the court to consider the aggravating circumstance` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 269.01(1) consider the fact that the victim was a public transit employee as an aggravating circumstance` AT 1
-- 269.1(2) "official means (a) a peace officer, (b) a public officer, (c) a member of the Canadian Forces, or (d) any person who may exercise powers, pursuant to a law in force in a foreign state, that would, in Canada, be exercised by a person referred to in paragraph (a), (b), or (c), whether the person exercises powers in Canada or outside Canada"
--                                      (a)           (b)           (c)           (d)
#ASSERT `s 269.1(2) official` (JUST TRUE)  (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 269.1(2) official` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE)  (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
